      "key": "SFCC-203",
      "summary": "PLP – Bottom Zone Editorial Slots — Contentful",
      "description": "As a\n Site Merchandiser, I want the PLP bottom zone editorial content managed in Contentful, so that I can configure and update the editorial blocks that appear below the product grid per category page without requiring a developer deployment.\nThis story is a follow-up to SFCC-82 (PLP UI – Bottom Zone Editorial Slots), which builds the PWA component shells with mock content. This story covers the Contentful content model and the integration between Contentful and the PWA Kit components so that all three editorial block variants are fully content-managed. A Site Merchandiser should be able to configure per category page:\nFull-width editorial image block:\n full-bleed image, caption text, and CTA link destination\nEditorial feature block:\n large image, optional product tile reference, title, description, and CTA link destination\nTwo-column content block:\n two independently configurable panels, each with image, title, description, and CTA link destination\nNo editorial slot:\n ability to leave the bottom zone empty for a given category",
