      "summary": "PDP – Product Badges — Merchandiser Configuration",
      "description": "As a\n Site Merchandiser, \nI want\n to create, assign, and manage product badges (such as Runway, Campaign, Exclusive, Online Exclusive, and VIC Exclusive) without code deployment, \nso that\n I can keep badge content accurate and up to date across all storefronts.\nThis story is the merchandiser counterpart to SFCC-132 (PDP UI – Product Badges), which builds the PWA component that renders badges on the PDP. \nThis story covers:\nCreating and naming badge types in BM (confirmed that badges are not coming from AP21)\nAssigning one or more badges to a product in BM\nConfiguring the priority hierarchy that determines display order when multiple badges apply, and being able to reorder this without a code change.\nFor initial build - we can configure it as Runway (1) > Campaign (2) > Exclusive (3) but this should be configurable\nLinking each badge to its corresponding category PLP URL\nSupporting locale-specific badge labels (e.g. translated labels per storefront locale)\nRegion-aware badge visibility (a badge may apply on some storefronts but not others)",
